            "notes": "##**Items & powers** \nIf you have a few bad match-ups against you, go with  [Power Playbook](item_6d8803cf-baa7-46ee-af91-51e7f2301418),  [Winning Attitude](item_8714087c-c078-4619-a2ef-327bc6edaa69), and  [Charged Plating](item_b8ca58e7-6ae2-40ee-8618-fe2f32315295). If you only have one bad match-up or no bad match-ups, keep  [Power Playbook](item_6d8803cf-baa7-46ee-af91-51e7f2301418) and take  [Shady Spectacles](item_ef9bb72f-a56c-4fb6-a552-5abce0b943d7) as well as  [Armored Vest](item_358361e2-59be-4c81-b221-8a87f37809e6) \n\n##**Playstyle**\n\nIf you have the first item combo mentioned above, your goal will be to flank and trade your life for a support or an annoying dps player, and get a lot of damage on their tank occasionnally. This will allow you to farm cash as well as your ult pretty fast. You will mostly rely on your team to win fights, but it's fine to take a loss if you farmed cash well.\nFor the second item combo, try to play safer while still flanking and annoying their backline. Most of the time your targets will be unnaware squishy's, so after you kill them try to survive and go back in with your next barrage.\n\nFeel free to switch item combos if you like one playstyle more than the other, though I wouldn't recommend it if you have a few bad match-ups.",
